    "title": "Verizon to install fiber conduits",
    "text": "Verizon New England, which was awarded $1.2 million to build out its fiber network in Jamestown, has been given permission to lay underground conduits on five streets.\nThe town council gave unanimous approval Monday at its meeting. President Nancy Beye, Councilman Eddie Ross and Councilwomen Mary Meagher and Mary Glackin endorsed the request. Vice President Erik Brine was absent.\nThe affected streets are Meadow Lane, Gondola Avenue, Aquidneck Court, Collins Terrace and Wright Lane.\nThe approval is conditional on Verizon tunneling underneath the asphalt with no excavation.",
